# Open work vs git

- Until a Linear workspace is attached, open work lives in git (PRs and whitepaper process docs). When Linear exists, it owns open work and decisions; close when decided, not when a PR exists. Git still owns facts.
- Git = facts that would otherwise lie. One canonical file; pointers elsewhere.
- PRs preferred. Do not merge or push to `main`/`master` without explicit user approval.
- Do not file openKMS work on other Linear workspaces (`NEW`, `ONC`, `PER`).

## Do not

- Restate a decision in parent README and child docs in the same change.

## Do

- Edit the file that owns the fact, then bump the parent pin ([docs/pin-bump.md](docs/pin-bump.md)).
- Point to [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) and `../openkms-whitepaper/coordination/git-workflow.md`.
